# timerdemo: the Timer widget (5s timeout, 1s interval) driving Tea v2 under
# a real pty (S9).
#
# The view is ONE row: "<state><remaining>" — "run 5s" while counting down,
# "stop <frozen>" while paused, "over 0s" once timed out.  Key-driven header
# flips are deterministic needles; tick-timed countdown repaints are NEVER
# asserted (R4) — only the first paint and the event-driven "over" flip:
#   resize probe (sync)  \e[?25l\e[2Krun 5s\r\n
#   tick 1 (sleep 1s)    \e[1;1H\e[2Krun 4s   (no trailing \r\n)
#   s (stop)             \e[1;1H\e[2Kstop <frozen>s
#   s (start)            \e[1;1H\e[2Krun <frozen>s   (re-arms; the countdown
#                         resumes from the frozen value)
#   5th accepted tick     Timedout notice -> \e[1;1H\e[2Kover 0s
#                         (rejected ticks repaint nothing — skipRender)
#   q                     \e[?25h + exit 0 (TaskQuit scan)
# Escapes: \e[?25l hide cursor, \e[?25h show cursor.
expect \e[?25l
expect 5s\r\n
send s
expect \e[1;1H\e[2Kstop
send s
expect \e[1;1H\e[2Krun
expect \e[1;1H\e[2Kover 0s
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
